Where CORE owners expose tenant IDs as strings:

1. Verify actual source validators and historical data.
2. Confirm whether those values are canonical UUID serializations.
3. Perform strict parsing at the repository boundary.
4. Reject malformed values.
5. Never trim, guess, repair or silently generate a replacement ID.
6. Preserve the source-level representation when required.
7. Use canonical CORE-001 tenant ownership.
8. Use an existing owner-governed mapping if a legitimate non-UUID tenant identifier requires mapping.
9. Reject unmapped and conflicting identifiers.

