3. Verify the access token through the approved OIDC verifier.
4. Resolve trusted identity, account, tenant, organization and active membership through CORE-001.
5. Resolve the current canonical authentication epoch and relevant membership/tenant revisions.
6. Validate the durable session using B4 storage against the verified principal and current trusted context.
7. Apply shared rate-limit policy.
8. Resolve the canonical resource/action authorization decision through CORE-001.
9. Persist the required minimized audit event before the protected handler.
10. Execute the protected handler.
11. Reauthorize protected mutations immediately before mutation execution where the route policy requires it.

Exact ordering must be verified against the existing `api-security.ts` lifecycle and its tests. Do not silently rearrange middleware.

